# Repo structure (multi-site monorepo)

This repository builds **several deployed sites** from one tree (deployment convenience). Each site has its **own dev docs** — do not mix them.

## Sites and doc homes

| Site | Source | Dev docs | Audience |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Explorations website | `src/`, `public/`, `cypress/` | **`website-docs/`** (VitePress) | Primary — explorations, E-Components, video |
| Website docs | `website-docs/` | `website-docs/README.md` | LLMs and humans extending the explorations site |
| Docs hub (fleet landing) | `docs-hub/` | `docs-hub/README.md` | Entry card page only |
| MCP server docs | `mcp-docs/` | `mcp-docs/README.md` | Shipped MCP tools and setup |
| Roadmap | `roadmap/` | `roadmap/README.md` | Internal strategy / Phase 3 conceptualization |
| Community token | `community-token/` | `community-token/README.md` | Internal transparency mini-site |

Fleet overview for humans: [docs.feelyourprotocol.org](https://docs.feelyourprotocol.org).

## Rules when editing docs

1. **`website-docs/` is website-only.** Cover `src/`, explorations, E-Components, styling, video, and this VitePress site. Do **not** add build/dev instructions for roadmap, community-token, mcp-docs, or docs-hub here — link to that folder's README instead.
2. **Do not encourage contributions to internal sites.** Roadmap and community-token may be public, but their READMEs are maintainer-facing; do not invite drive-by PRs there in website-docs.
3. **Cross-links are fine; cross-docs are not.** Nav/footer may link to live URLs. Do not copy sibling-site dev content into website-docs.
4. **Shared constants** — fleet URLs live in `src/libs/docsUrls.ts` and `src/libs/roadmapUrls.ts`. The main site may reference roadmap URLs (e.g. banner); that is product wiring, not roadmap dev docs.

## Rules when editing code

- Explorations and shared UI → `src/`
- New exploration → `src/explorations/<id>/` per `website-docs/contributing/adding-an-exploration.md`
- Do not import from `community-token/`, `roadmap/`, or `mcp-docs/` into `src/` (except shared libs under `src/libs/` or `shared/`)
- Full deploy builds all targets (`npm run build:deploy`); when working on the explorations site, `npm run dev` and `npm run website:build` are enough

## Cursor rules catalog

`.cursor/rules/` should stay a **small, scalable set**. Prefer **task-focused names** (`testing.mdc`, `video-recording.mdc`) over tool- or command-specific ones.

**Core SWE primitives** (always-on, one concern each): `repo-structure.mdc`, `quality.mdc`, `testing.mdc`. Keep these generic enough to apply to any folder.

**Specialized task rules** (justified when the workflow is large and easy to get wrong): `video-recording.mdc`, `og-images.mdc`. Do **not** fold those into a primitive — and do not grow new always-on files for one-off commands.

New rules: same split. Put invariants in a primitive; put long capture/setup playbooks in a named task file.

## Direction of travel

Exploration creation is moving toward **LLM/agent automation** (including MCP integration). Prefer extending **`website-docs/`** and **`.cursor/rules/`** so agents can run end-to-end with minimal human steps.
